     The aaccll__ddeelleettee__eennttrryy() function returns the value 0 if successful; other‐
     wise the value -1 is returned and the global variable _e_r_r_n_o is set to in‐
     dicate the error.

EERRRROORRSS
     The aaccll__ddeelleettee__eennttrryy() function fails if:

     [EINVAL]           Argument _a_c_l does not point to a valid ACL.  Argument
                        _e_n_t_r_y___d is not a valid descriptor for an ACL entry in
                        _a_c_l.  Argument _i_n_d_e_x is out of bounds.

